---
import NoteFigure from './NoteFigure.astro';
---

<NoteFigure
  label="Architecture sketch"
  title="Learned channel mixing with a simple determinant"
  caption="The channel-mixing sketch on page 37 is expanded using the Glow paper's LU parameterization and flow step. At one pixel, the exact example W = [[2, 1], [1, 1]] maps the unit square to a parallelogram of area 1; a general learned W need not preserve volume. An image applies the same matrix at H × W positions. The seminar notebook instead mixes two-dimensional points, without that spatial multiplier. These are algebraic illustrations, not measured training results."
>
  <div class="glow-panels">
    <svg viewBox="0 0 360 430" role="img" aria-labelledby="flow-glow-mix-title flow-glow-mix-desc">
      <title id="flow-glow-mix-title">A one-by-one convolution mixes channels at the same pixel</title>
      <desc id="flow-glow-mix-desc">Two input channels u one and u two at a fixed pixel are mapped to two u one plus u two, and u one plus u two. The example matrix has rows two one and one one, and determinant one. Its columns map the first basis vector to two one and the second to one one. The unit square becomes a parallelogram with the same area, although this is not a requirement for a general Glow channel-mixing matrix.</desc>
      <defs>
        <marker id="flow-glow-mix-arrow" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="8" refY="5" markerWidth="5" markerHeight="5" orient="auto-start-reverse">
          <path d="M 1 1 L 8 5 L 1 9" class="accent-arrow" />
        </marker>
        <marker id="flow-glow-second-arrow" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="8" refY="5" markerWidth="5" markerHeight="5" orient="auto-start-reverse">
          <path d="M 1 1 L 8 5 L 1 9" class="ink-arrow" />
        </marker>
      </defs>
      <text x="180" y="22" text-anchor="middle" class="panel-title">One pixel, two channels</text>
      <text x="180" y="45" text-anchor="middle" class="muted">Same spatial position (r, c)</text>
      <rect x="16" y="64" width="113" height="69" rx="5" class="box" />
      <rect x="237" y="64" width="107" height="69" rx="5" class="box" />
      <text x="72" y="89" text-anchor="middle">u₁</text>
      <text x="72" y="116" text-anchor="middle">u₂</text>
      <text x="291" y="89" text-anchor="middle" class="accent">2u₁ + u₂</text>
      <text x="291" y="116" text-anchor="middle" class="accent">u₁ + u₂</text>
      <path d="M 137 104 H 228" class="accent-arrow" marker-end="url(#flow-glow-mix-arrow)" />
      <text x="182" y="88" text-anchor="middle">W</text>
      <text x="72" y="153" text-anchor="middle" class="muted">input channels</text>
      <text x="291" y="153" text-anchor="middle" class="muted">output channels</text>
      <text x="180" y="181" text-anchor="middle">W = [2 1; 1 1], det W = 1</text>

      <text x="24" y="210" class="muted">channel 2</text>
      <path d="M 54 220 V 350 H 270" class="axis" />
      <path d="M 54 350 H 109 V 295 H 54 Z" class="unit-square" />
      <path d="M 54 350 L 164 295 L 219 240 L 109 295 Z" class="mapped-square" />
      <path d="M 54 350 L 164 295" class="accent-arrow basis-vector" marker-end="url(#flow-glow-mix-arrow)" />
      <path d="M 54 350 L 109 295" class="ink-arrow basis-vector" marker-end="url(#flow-glow-second-arrow)" />
      <circle cx="54" cy="350" r="2.5" class="origin" />
      {[1, 2, 3].map((tick) => (
        <g>
          <path d={`M ${54 + 55 * tick} 350 v 4`} class="axis" />
          <text x={54 + 55 * tick} y="373" text-anchor="middle" class="muted">{tick}</text>
        </g>
      ))}
      {[1, 2].map((tick) => (
        <g>
          <path d={`M 50 ${350 - 55 * tick} h 4`} class="axis" />
          <text x="39" y={354 - 55 * tick} text-anchor="end" class="muted">{tick}</text>
        </g>
      ))}
      <text x="266" y="393" text-anchor="end" class="muted">channel 1</text>
      <text x="172" y="315" class="accent">We₁ = (2, 1)</text>
      <text x="17" y="261">We₂ = (1, 1)</text>
      <path d="M 77 268 L 104 286" class="guide" />
      <text x="160" y="274" text-anchor="middle" class="accent">area 1</text>
      <path d="M 30 416 H 55" class="unit-square" />
      <text x="62" y="420" class="muted">unit square</text>
      <path d="M 185 416 H 210" class="outline" />
      <text x="217" y="420" class="muted">mapped square</text>
    </svg>

    <svg viewBox="0 0 360 430" role="img" aria-labelledby="flow-glow-lu-title flow-glow-lu-desc">
      <title id="flow-glow-lu-title">LU factors reduce the channel-mixing log determinant to a diagonal sum</title>
      <desc id="flow-glow-lu-desc">Glow writes W as P times L times the sum of U and diagonal a. P is a fixed permutation, L has unit diagonal, U is strictly upper triangular, and every a entry is nonzero. For the example W, P is identity, L has lower-left entry one half, and the upper factor has diagonal two and one half. Across H times W image positions the contribution is H W times the sum of log absolute a. A complete Glow step applies ActNorm, invertible one-by-one channel mixing and affine coupling; their log determinants add.</desc>
      <defs>
        <marker id="flow-glow-step-arrow" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="8" refY="5" markerWidth="5" markerHeight="5" orient="auto-start-reverse">
          <path d="M 1 1 L 8 5 L 1 9" class="accent-arrow" />
        </marker>
      </defs>
      <text x="180" y="22" text-anchor="middle" class="panel-title">W = P L (U + diag a)</text>
      <text x="180" y="45" text-anchor="middle" class="muted">Factors of the example matrix</text>
      <rect x="15" y="64" width="76" height="73" rx="5" class="box" />
      <rect x="123" y="64" width="83" height="73" rx="5" class="box" />
      <rect x="238" y="64" width="107" height="73" rx="5" class="box" />
      <text x="39" y="93" text-anchor="middle">1</text>
      <text x="67" y="93" text-anchor="middle">0</text>
      <text x="39" y="119" text-anchor="middle">0</text>
      <text x="67" y="119" text-anchor="middle">1</text>
      <text x="145" y="93" text-anchor="middle" class="accent">1</text>
      <text x="183" y="93" text-anchor="middle">0</text>
      <text x="145" y="119" text-anchor="middle">½</text>
      <text x="183" y="119" text-anchor="middle" class="accent">1</text>
      <text x="265" y="93" text-anchor="middle" class="accent diagonal">2</text>
      <text x="316" y="93" text-anchor="middle">1</text>
      <text x="265" y="119" text-anchor="middle">0</text>
      <text x="316" y="119" text-anchor="middle" class="accent diagonal">½</text>
      <text x="107" y="105" text-anchor="middle" class="muted">×</text>
      <text x="222" y="105" text-anchor="middle" class="muted">×</text>
      <text x="53" y="157" text-anchor="middle" class="muted">P = I</text>
      <text x="165" y="157" text-anchor="middle" class="muted">unit diagonal</text>
      <text x="292" y="157" text-anchor="middle" class="muted">a = (2, ½)</text>
      <text x="180" y="187" text-anchor="middle" class="accent">General layer: every aᵢ ≠ 0</text>
      <text x="180" y="222" text-anchor="middle" class="formula">HW Σᵢ log |aᵢ|</text>
      <text x="180" y="246" text-anchor="middle" class="muted">H × W positions share the same W</text>
      <text x="180" y="268" text-anchor="middle" class="muted">P and unit-diagonal L add zero</text>

      <text x="180" y="307" text-anchor="middle" class="panel-title">One Glow step</text>
      <rect x="15" y="329" width="91" height="49" rx="5" class="box" />
      <rect x="134" y="329" width="94" height="49" rx="5" class="box" />
      <rect x="256" y="329" width="89" height="49" rx="5" class="box" />
      <text x="60" y="350" text-anchor="middle">ActNorm</text>
      <text x="60" y="369" text-anchor="middle" class="muted">scale + bias</text>
      <text x="181" y="350" text-anchor="middle">1 × 1 mix</text>
      <text x="181" y="369" text-anchor="middle" class="muted">learned W</text>
      <text x="300" y="350" text-anchor="middle">affine</text>
      <text x="300" y="369" text-anchor="middle">coupling</text>
      <path d="M 111 354 H 127" class="accent-arrow" marker-end="url(#flow-glow-step-arrow)" />
      <path d="M 233 354 H 249" class="accent-arrow" marker-end="url(#flow-glow-step-arrow)" />
      <text x="180" y="403" text-anchor="middle" class="muted">The step's log-determinants add</text>
      <text x="180" y="425" text-anchor="middle" class="footnote">Paper context; notebook uses spline coupling</text>
    </svg>
  </div>
</NoteFigure>

<style>
  .glow-panels { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 1.5rem; }
  svg { display: block; width: 100%; max-width: 380px; height: auto; margin-inline: auto; }
  text { fill: var(--ink); font-family: var(--sans); font-size: 14px; }
  .panel-title { font-size: 15px; font-weight: 600; }
  .muted { fill: var(--muted); font-size: 13px; }
  .footnote { fill: var(--muted); font-size: 12px; }
  .accent { fill: var(--accent); }
  .diagonal { font-weight: 700; }
  .formula { fill: var(--accent); font-size: 18px; }
  .box { fill: none; stroke: var(--line); stroke-width: 1.2; }
  .axis { fill: none; stroke: var(--line); stroke-width: 1; }
  .guide { fill: none; stroke: var(--muted); stroke-width: 1; }
  .unit-square { fill: none; stroke: var(--muted); stroke-width: 1.2; stroke-dasharray: 4 3; }
  .mapped-square { fill: var(--accent); fill-opacity: 0.06; stroke: var(--accent); stroke-width: 1.5; }
  .outline { fill: none; stroke: var(--accent); stroke-width: 1.5; }
  .accent-arrow, .ink-arrow { fill: none; stroke-width: 1.4; stroke-linecap: round; stroke-linejoin: round; }
  .accent-arrow { stroke: var(--accent); }
  .ink-arrow { stroke: var(--ink); }
  .basis-vector { stroke-width: 1.8; }
  .origin { fill: var(--ink); }
  @container (max-width: 580px) { .glow-panels { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 2rem; } }
</style>
